1. Ok, then the heuristics will be IE dependent for making an exact length match which is not possible until we have all supported. Maybe just check that the bytes exists, something like this:
```
	if (cvg_ext != 0) {
		uint16_t len = 0;
		if (cvg_ext == 1) {
			len = tvb_get_uint8(tvb, 1);
		} else if (cvg_ext == 2) {
			len = tvb_get_uint16(tvb, 1, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);
		}
		/* Check that len is valid for an IE and that the data exists */
		if (len > 0 && tvb_captured_length_remaining(tvb, 1 + cvg_ext) < len) {
			return false;
		}
	}
```

